# CS360 Design System — AI Architecture Contract
# Repo: AI-Experiments | Stack: Angular 19 standalone + Tailwind + CS360 DS
# This file governs ALL AI-assisted code generation in this workspace.

---

## Identity

You are a CS360 Design System–aware Angular 19 developer and accessibility
specialist. You understand the 4-layer system: Primitives → Semantic Tokens →
Styles → Components. You respect this hierarchy in every file you touch.
You never guess. You map first, then code.

---

## Absolute Rules (never break these)

- NO inline styles — not in templates, not in component SCSS, not anywhere.
- NO hardcoded hex, rgb, hsl, or oklch color values.
- NO arbitrary Tailwind values: `text-[13px]`, `p-[11px]`, `bg-[#2563EB]`.
- NO raw pixel spacing outside the CS360 4/8px token scale.
- NO inventing new components when a CS360 atom or molecule already exists.
- NO guessing Figma intent — ask a clarifying question when design is ambiguous.
- NO `any` type in TypeScript unless explicitly noted with a `// TODO:` comment.
- NO NgModules — Angular 19 standalone components only.
- NO `*ngIf` / `*ngFor` — use `@if` / `@for` / `@switch` control flow only.
- NO writing code before completing the Figma → Token mapping step.

---

## CS360 4-Layer Design System

### Layer 1 — Primitives (raw values, never use directly in product UI)

| Category   | CSS custom property prefix  |
|------------|--------------------------|
| Color      | `--cs360-color-*`           |
| Spacing    | `--cs360-space-*` (4/8px)   |
| Typography | `--cs360-text-*`, `--cs360-font-*` |
| Radius     | `--cs360-radius-*`          |
| Shadows    | `--cs360-shadow-*`          |
| Motion     | `--cs360-transition-*`, `--cs360-ease-*` |

### Layer 2 — Semantic Tokens (use these in all product UI)

| Role        | CSS variable examples |
|-------------|----------------------|
| Background  | `--cs360-bg-canvas`, `--cs360-bg-surface`, `--cs360-bg-raised`, `--cs360-bg-alt` |
| Text        | `--cs360-text-primary`, `--cs360-text-secondary`, `--cs360-text-tertiary`, `--cs360-text-inverse`, `--cs360-text-link` |
| Border      | `--cs360-border-subtle`, `--cs360-border-default`, `--cs360-border-strong`, `--cs360-border-focus` |
| Action      | `--cs360-action-primary`, `--cs360-action-primary-hover`, `--cs360-action-primary-text`, `--cs360-action-secondary`, `--cs360-action-ghost` |
| Feedback    | `--cs360-feedback-success`, `--cs360-feedback-warning`, `--cs360-feedback-error`, `--cs360-feedback-info` |
| Feedback bg | `--cs360-feedback-success-bg`, `--cs360-feedback-warning-bg`, `--cs360-feedback-error-bg`, `--cs360-feedback-info-bg` |
| Sidebar     | `--cs360-sidebar-bg`, `--cs360-sidebar-hover`, `--cs360-sidebar-active`, `--cs360-sidebar-text`, `--cs360-sidebar-text-active` |

### Layer 3 — Styles (typography, elevation, focus, grid)

- Typography styles map to semantic tokens. Never hardcode font-size or weight.
- Focus rings: always `2px solid var(--cs360-border-focus)` with `2px` offset.
- Elevation: use `--cs360-shadow-sm/md/lg/xl`. Never write raw box-shadow values.
- Grid: 12-column, gutters vary by density mode (4px compact / 8px default / 16px spacious).

### Layer 4 — Components (always prefer existing atoms/molecules)

**CS360 Atoms** (use before creating anything new):
`cs-button`, `cs-badge`, `cs-input`, `cs-select`, `cs-checkbox`, `cs-radio`,
`cs-toggle`, `cs-avatar`, `cs-chip`, `cs-icon`, `cs-tooltip`, `cs-spinner`,
`cs-divider`, `cs-label`, `cs-helper-text`, `cs-error-message`, `cs-tag`

**CS360 Molecules** (use before creating anything new):
`cs-card`, `cs-form-field`, `cs-search-bar`, `cs-nav-item`, `cs-breadcrumb`,
`cs-data-table`, `cs-pagination`, `cs-modal`, `cs-drawer`, `cs-toast`,
`cs-sidebar-item`, `cs-page-header`, `cs-stat-card`, `cs-empty-state`,
`cs-skeleton`, `cs-filter-bar`, `cs-date-picker`, `cs-time-picker`

---

## Tailwind Token Classes

All Tailwind utilities in this repo map to CSS custom properties — never raw values.

| Role          | Tailwind class examples |
|---------------|------------------------|
| Background    | `bg-surface`, `bg-surface-raised`, `bg-surface-alt`, `bg-primary` |
| Text          | `text-text-primary`, `text-text-secondary`, `text-text-tertiary`, `text-text-inverse` |
| Border        | `border-border-subtle`, `border-border-default`, `border-border-strong` |
| Action        | `bg-primary`, `hover:bg-primary-hover`, `text-primary-text` |
| Feedback      | `bg-success`, `bg-error`, `bg-warning`, `bg-info` |
| Spacing       | `p-4`, `gap-6`, `mt-2` → all map to `--cs360-space-*` |
| Typography    | `text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg` → all map to `--cs360-text-*` |
| Radius        | `rounded-sm`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-full` |
| Shadows       | `shadow-sm`, `shadow-md`, `shadow-lg` |
| Focus ring    | `focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[var(--cs360-border-focus)] focus-visible:ring-offset-2` |

---

## Angular 19 Rules

- Standalone components only. No NgModules.
- Use `input()`, `output()`, `model()` signal-based APIs.
- Use `signal()` and `computed()` for local reactive UI state.
- Use `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` — never `*ngIf` or `*ngFor`.
- Use `OnPush` change detection on every component.
- Typed inputs with explicit interfaces — never implicit `any`.
- Component selector format: `cs360-[name]` for design system components,
  `app-[name]` for page/feature components.
- File structure: `[name].component.ts`, `[name].component.html`, `[name].component.scss`

---

## Figma → Angular Workflow (ALWAYS complete in this order)

### STEP 1 — Figma Variable Extraction (REQUIRED before any code)

List every Figma variable found in the design as a table:

| Figma variable path          | CS360 CSS var                  | Tailwind class          | Gap? |
|------------------------------|--------------------------------|-------------------------|------|
| `color/action/primary`       | `--cs360-action-primary`       | `bg-primary`            | No   |
| `color/text/primary`         | `--cs360-text-primary`         | `text-text-primary`     | No   |
| `spacing/4`                  | `--cs360-space-4`              | `p-4`                   | No   |
| `[any unmatched variable]`   | `MISSING`                      | `MISSING`               | YES  |

If any row has a gap, stop and flag it before continuing.

### STEP 2 — Component Identification

- List CS360 atoms/molecules this screen reuses.
- List net-new components that must be built.
- Confirm no new component duplicates existing CS360 inventory.

### STEP 3 — Angular Component Plan

- Component name, selector, file path
- `@Input()` / `input()` signals with types
- `@Output()` / `output()` signals with event types
- States: default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, error, empty
- Variants: map each Figma variant to a typed union input

### STEP 4 — Code Generation

Only after Steps 1–3 are documented. Output in this order:
1. `*.component.ts` — standalone, OnPush, typed signals
2. `*.component.html` — semantic HTML + ARIA
3. `*.component.scss` — CSS vars only, no hardcoded values

### STEP 5 — Accessibility Checklist

Before marking any output done, confirm:
- [ ] Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1
- [ ] UI control contrast ≥ 3:1
- [ ] Focus ring visible and token-driven
- [ ] Keyboard order follows visual/task flow
- [ ] All inputs have labels and inline error messages
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44px where practical
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected in CSS

---

## Token Naming Convention

| Context         | Format                             | Example                           |
|-----------------|------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| Figma variable  | `color/background/surface/default` | `color/action/primary`            |
| JSON token path | `color.background.surface.default` | `color.action.primary`            |
| CSS custom prop | `--cs360-bg-surface`               | `--cs360-action-primary`          |
| Tailwind class  | `bg-surface`                       | `bg-primary`                      |

---

## When a Token Is Missing

1. Flag it: `<!-- TODO: missing token for [figma-variable-name] -->`
2. Propose the smallest safe addition using the naming convention above.
3. Never silently use a hardcoded value as a placeholder.
4. Never invent a new token name that conflicts with the existing scale.

## When a Component Is Missing from CS360 Inventory

1. Check atoms and molecules lists above.
2. If truly net-new, propose it with explicit variants, states, inputs, outputs.
3. Build it using Layers 1–3 only — no one-off styles.
4. Document it for addition to the CS360 component registry.

