## Figma Annotation System — AI Instruction Contract
# Updated: 2026-06-01 | Caregiver Web Portal (XCvAxa7G7QgiTfk08G2LGg)
# This section governs how ALL AI tools must READ and USE Figma annotations.

---

### What Figma Annotations Are (in this project)

Annotations are typed, categorised text blocks attached to specific Figma layers in Dev Mode.
They provide INTENT and BEHAVIOUR that Figma's inspect data alone cannot carry.
Every AI tool (Cursor, Claude, Copilot, Perplexity/Comet, Antigravity) MUST read annotations
before generating any code from a Figma design.

Figma MCP server (`figma-developer-mcp`) delivers annotations as part of the node context.
They appear under `annotations[]` on each node returned by `get_figma_data` or `get_code`.

---

### Annotation Categories — What Each Means

| Category      | Read it for                                                      |
|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Development   | Component selector, API endpoints, data model, Angular @Inputs   |
| Interaction   | State machine, hover/focus/active/disabled, transitions, events  |
| Accessibility | ARIA roles, labels, keyboard nav, screen reader behaviour        |
| Content       | Dynamic text binding, format rules, fallback values, i18n notes  |
| AI            | Direct code-gen prompt, MCP-specific instructions, edge cases    |

---

### Annotation Reading Rules (MANDATORY for all AI tools)

1. ALWAYS read `Development` annotation before writing any component code.
   It overrides anything you infer from the layer tree alone.

2. ALWAYS read `Interaction` annotation before writing event handlers, animations, or state logic.
   Do not invent interaction patterns — if it is not in the annotation, ask.

3. Only write ARIA if an `Accessibility` annotation is present AND explicit.
   Do not auto-generate ARIA from guesses.

4. Use `Content` annotation for exact text bindings, format patterns, and fallback strings.
   Do not hardcode any visible string unless the Content annotation confirms it is static.

5. An `AI` category annotation is a direct prompt fragment — treat it as an addendum
   to your current system instruction for that component.

6. If NO annotation exists on a node, fetch data from Figma inspect (tokens, layout, variants)
   and flag any behavioural uncertainty in a `// TODO:` comment in the generated code.

---

### What Annotations DO NOT Replace (DO NOT re-fetch)

Do NOT ask for or re-describe these — Figma MCP fetches them automatically:
- Token names (color, spacing, radius, typography variables)
- Auto Layout values (gap, padding, direction, alignment)
- Component variant properties (Type=Default, Size=M, State=Hover)
- Layer dimensions, fill colors bound to variables
- Child component names and hierarchy

Annotations ONLY carry what MCP cannot: intent, transitions, API endpoints, business rules.

