### Annotation Decision Rule — Write vs Skip

WRITE an annotation when:
- A behaviour or rule is NOT visible in the Figma layer tree
- A transition timing, animation, or collapsed state needs specifying
- An API endpoint, HTTP method, or payload shape must be used
- A business rule governs display (e.g. "only show Clock-Out when isOngoing=true")
- A fallback/empty/error state needs defining
- ARIA that is non-obvious must be specified

SKIP an annotation when:
- The information is already in Figma variables, tokens, or variant properties
- The information is derivable from the layer name + Auto Layout values
- It would duplicate what Figma MCP already returns in inspect data

---

### MCP Prompt Usage

When implementing a Figma frame via MCP:
1. Select the frame in Figma Dev Mode
2. Check Estimated tokens (keep under 40k for best results; split large frames)
3. Click "Copy example prompt" in the MCP panel
4. Paste into your AI agent (Claude / Cursor / Copilot)
5. The agent MUST read all annotations on that frame before generating code
6. Token budget warning at 47k+ — select sub-components individually

Active MCP connections (verified 2026-06-01):
- Figma Developer MCP (VS Code)      ✓ Active
- Anima (Figma → Angular/React/HTML) ✓ Active
- Jira integration                   ✓ Active
- Stark (Accessibility checker)      ✓ Saved
- Figma to Code (HTML/Tailwind/Flutter/SwiftUI) ✓ Running

---

### One-Annotation-Per-Concern Rule

Each annotation = one typed concern = one category.
Never write a prose blob across multiple concerns in one annotation.
Bad:  "This is the sidenav. Height is fill. It has expanded and collapsed states.
       Follow the component. Add localStorage."
Good: [Development] Collapsed width: 48px. Collapse trigger: nav-footer-collapse-btn.
      [Interaction]  Width transition: ease-in-out 200ms on container only.
                     State persists in localStorage key: cs360_nav_expanded.

The rule: every annotation is a pre-written typed prompt fragment for the AI
agent that will implement this component.

